===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# The steep artificial slope below a [[fort]]'s [[parapet]].
# {{lb|en|geology}} A cliff at the edge of a [[plateau]] or [[ridge]] caused by [[erosion]] or faulting; the steeper side of an [[escarpment]].
#* '''2014,''' {{w|Paul Salopek}}, ''Blessed. Cursed. Claimed.'', National Geographic (December 2014)[https://web.archive.org/web/20150212214621/http://ngm.nationalgeographic.com/2014/12/pilgrim-roads/salopek-text]
#*: {{quote|en|Sweating under the sun, we scale the barren eastern '''scarp''' of the Great Rift Valley (Area B), edging carefully around controversial, razor-wired Israeli settlements (Area C).}}
# {{lb|en|heraldry}} {{obsolete spelling of|en|scrape|scarpe, scrape}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1673|author=Matthew Carter|title=Honor Redivivus: Or, The Analysis of Honor and Armory|page=211
|text=[...] as in the seventh, which is Argent a '''Scarp''' Azure.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1724|author=John Guillim|title=A Display of Heraldry|page=38
|text=He beareth Argent, a '''Scarp''', Azure.}}

